# Form validation before the request

Check every user-entered field in the view **before** the ViewModel or repository calls the server. The server still rejects bad input. The UI must not use that rejection as the first check.

## How

- Put checks in `lib/core/errors/form_validators.dart` for that app. Match the server rule (required, length, email, phone, money).
- Show the message on the field (`validator` or `AppTextField.error`), in en/ar/fr. Do not use one generic banner for a known field.
- `FormState.validate()` or the field-error map runs in the submit handler. Return before `ref.read(...).save()` / repository call when any field fails.
- A server error after a valid submit stays a banner, or on the field when the code names that field.

```dart
onPressed: () async {
  final emailError = FormValidators.email(l10n, email.text);
  setState(() => _emailError = emailError);
  if (emailError != null) return;
  await ref.read(authViewModelProvider.notifier).login(email.text.trim(), password.text);
}
```

Search and taps that are not data entry do not need a form. Do not add a client check the server does not have.
